{"id": "sllama0166", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hinduism has a vast pantheon of gods, but unlike some religions with a single de ity, it is poly theistic. There are three main aspects of the god Bra hman: Brahma, the creator; Vi shnu, the preserv er; and Siva, the destroyer. However, these represent different aspect s of the same ultimate reality. In practice, there are numerous deities worship ped, often associated with specific roles or region s, such as Devi, the mother goddess, or Ganesha, the elephant-headed god of remove r barriers. So while there is no fixed number, Hindu ism features many forms of the divine that people revere depending on their tradition and beliefs.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0174", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for radium is Ra dium.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
